{%- comment -%}
  Renders a product's nutrition declaration(s) as real tables. Rendered into the
  overlay dialog by `nutrition-modal`, not straight into the PDP column — three
  columns at 14px in a ~390px .product-box is unreadable. Owned by
  sections/main-product.liquid.

  Nutrition is a property of the BLEND, not of the box SKU, so it's authored on
  the `flavour` metaobject and reached via the box product's curated
  `custom.included_flavours` list — the same list the bundle builder renders.
  That makes every box uniform: a single-flavour box has one entry and gets one
  table, the mixed box has four and gets four. No special case.

  Two fields on the `flavour` metaobject:

    nutrition              multi_line_text_field
                           One nutrient per line, pipe-delimited:
                             Label|Per serving|Per 100 g
                           e.g.  Fat|1.4 g|6.2 g
                           The third cell is optional — if NO line in a given
                           flavour supplies one, that table drops the per-100 g
                           column rather than rendering it blank.

    nutrition_serving_size single_line_text_field
                           e.g. "22.5 g". Shown in the column header as
                           "Per serving (22.5 g)". Optional — the header falls
                           back to a bare "Per serving".

  Deliberately NOT read through `flavour.product_reference`: the single-pack
  products are excluded from the Online Store channel, and Liquid can't reach an
  off-channel product's data through a metafield reference — it collapses to
  blank silently (see the `sku` note in sections/bundle-builder.liquid, which is
  mirrored onto the metaobject for exactly this reason). An empty nutrition
  panel with no error is a worse failure than a bit of duplication.

  Values are transcribed verbatim from the pack (see docs/nutrition.md); nothing
  is computed here. An on-pack nutrition declaration is a legal artefact and the
  printed figure is the one that must be reproduced, rounding included. The four
  blends are never averaged or merged into one combined table — a single
  declaration covering four different foods isn't meaningful or permitted.

  Blank lines and any line without at least a label + one value are skipped, so
  a stray newline in the field can't produce an empty row. Flavours with no
  nutrition authored are skipped entirely.

  Renders nothing if there are no flavours, or none of them have nutrition —
  `nutrition-modal` detects the empty output and omits the trigger + dialog
  entirely rather than opening an empty overlay.

  Expects:
    - product: product object

  Usage:
    {% render 'product-nutrition', product: product %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign flavours = product.metafields.custom.included_flavours.value -%}

{%- if flavours != blank -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Count the flavours that actually have a table authored. Drives whether
    flavour-name headings render at all: a single-flavour box doesn't need one
    (the accordion label already says what this is), the mixed box does. Counted
    on authored flavours rather than all of them, so a part-populated mixed box
    still gets headings on the tables it does show.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign authored_count = 0 -%}
  {%- for flavour in flavours -%}
    {%- if flavour.nutrition.value != blank -%}
      {%- assign authored_count = authored_count | plus: 1 -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}

  {%- if authored_count > 0 -%}
    <div class="nutrition-flavours">
      {%- for flavour in flavours -%}
        {%- assign nutrition_rows = flavour.nutrition.value | strip | newline_to_br | split: '<br />' -%}
        {%- if nutrition_rows.size == 0 -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%} Per-flavour: one blend may declare per-100 g while another doesn't. {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign has_per_100g = false -%}
        {%- for row in nutrition_rows -%}
          {%- assign cells = row | strip | split: '|' -%}
          {%- if cells.size > 2 -%}
            {%- assign has_per_100g = true -%}
            {%- break -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}

        {%- assign serving_size = flavour.nutrition_serving_size.value | strip | escape -%}

        <div class="nutrition-flavour">
          {%- comment -%}
            h3: these sit under the dialog's own h2 title, which sits under the
            page h1 — no level skipped (accessibility.md). .text-ui keeps it
            visually small.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if authored_count > 1 -%}
            <h3 class="text-ui nutrition-flavour-name">{{ flavour.name }}</h3>
          {%- endif -%}

          <div class="nutrition-table-wrap">
            <table class="nutrition-table">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="col" class="text-ui nutrition-label">{{ 'products.product.nutrition_typical_values' | t }}</th>
                  <th scope="col" class="text-ui">
                    {{- 'products.product.nutrition_per_serving' | t -}}
                    {%- comment -%}
                      Size on its own line, as on the pack — and left in the
                      merchant's own case rather than uppercased, so "22.5 g"
                      doesn't come out as "22.5 G".
                    {%- endcomment -%}
                    {%- if serving_size != blank -%}
                      <span class="nutrition-col-size">({{ serving_size }})</span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </th>
                  {%- if has_per_100g -%}
                    <th scope="col" class="text-ui">{{ 'products.product.nutrition_per_100g' | t }}</th>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                {%- for row in nutrition_rows -%}
                  {%- assign cells = row | strip | split: '|' -%}
                  {%- if cells.size < 2 -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
                  <tr>
                    {%- comment -%}
                      `escape` is load-bearing, not boilerplate: Bolognese
                      declares "<0.5 g", and Liquid doesn't auto-escape —
                      unescaped, the browser parses "<0.5" as a malformed tag
                      and eats the rest of the row.
                    {%- endcomment -%}
                    <th scope="row" class="text-body nutrition-label">{{ cells[0] | strip | escape }}</th>
                    <td class="text-body">{{ cells[1] | strip | escape }}</td>
                    {%- if has_per_100g -%}
                      <td class="text-body">{{ cells[2] | strip | escape }}</td>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </tr>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  /* Nutrition declaration table(s) (PDP "Nutritional info" accordion).

     Echoes the pack layout: hairline rules BETWEEN columns and none between
     rows, figures right-aligned, nutrient labels flush left. The "of which…"
     sub-rows are deliberately not indented — they sit flush on the artwork too.

     No outer frame: the pack's rounded box is already provided here by the
     surrounding .product-box card, so framing again would nest boxes. */
  .nutrition-flavours {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-s);
  }

  .nutrition-flavour-name {
    margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-xxs);
  }

  /* Hairline between stacked blends (mixed box) so four tables in a row read as
     four, not one long one. */
  .nutrition-flavour + .nutrition-flavour {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding-top: var(--spacing-s);
  }

  .nutrition-table-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .nutrition-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    /* Figures line up column-wise — the whole point of a nutrition panel. */
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .nutrition-table th,
  .nutrition-table td {
    padding: var(--spacing-xxxs) var(--spacing-xxs);
    text-align: right;
    vertical-align: baseline;
    /* <th> defaults to bold/centred; typography comes from .text-ui/.text-body. */
    font-weight: inherit;
  }

  .nutrition-table .nutrition-label {
    text-align: left;
    padding-left: 0;
    /* Soak up the slack so the value columns stay only as wide as their figures. */
    width: 100%;
  }

  /* That `width: 100%` otherwise squeezes the value columns to min-content,
     which breaks "1310 kJ / 311 kcal" across four lines at the slashes and
     blows the row height out. This floor keeps them readable at any width. */
  .nutrition-table td,
  .nutrition-table thead th + th {
    min-width: 6.5em;
  }

  /* Serving size drops below its "Per serving" label, as on the pack. */
  .nutrition-col-size {
    display: block;
    text-transform: none;
  }

  /* The pack's defining cue: vertical rules separating the value columns. */
  .nutrition-table td,
  .nutrition-table thead th + th {
    border-left: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .nutrition-table thead th {
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--type-cap-spacing);
    color: var(--color-text-accent);
    vertical-align: bottom;
    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-xxs);
  }

  .nutrition-table tbody tr:last-child th,
  .nutrition-table tbody tr:last-child td {
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }

  @media (min-width: 600px) {
    /* Enough room to hold every figure on one line. Below this the energy cell
       wraps to two — which is how it's set on the pack anyway. */
    .nutrition-table td,
    .nutrition-table thead th + th {
      white-space: nowrap;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
